cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use listener in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "listener: verified loudness measures, conformance fixtures and a benchmark of published loudness phenomena for sound effects"
abstract: >-
  listener supports research on how loud sound effects are heard. It computes
  ITU-R BS.1770, ISO 532-1, DIN 45692 and ECMA-418-2 measures per file and per
  sound event at stated playback levels, checks them against the standards'
  test signals, reports where the measures disagree on a corpus in dB of gain,
  and scores every measure against published results on the loudness of short
  and changing sounds. It prepares a listening test and an event-level
  loudness model fitted to its data.
authors:
  - family-names: Sandner
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1041-814X"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/eigensoundlab/listener"
keywords:
  - loudness
  - psychoacoustics
  - sound effects
  - ITU-R BS.1770
  - ISO 532-1
  - ECMA-418-2
  - listening tests
  - game audio
  - sound design
  - conformance testing
